{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrudDZAXnWCkJD1s3zED","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Issue #1146 is fixed. `get_metadata_for_wheel()` now reads only `{name}-{version}.dist-info/METADATA` from the wheel, so a vendored `.dist-info` earlier in the zip is ignored. The 80 targeted tests pass (2 skipped), and ruff is clean on the changed files. Nothing is committed.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/fromager/pkgmetadata/pep376.py`** (new): `verbatim_dist_name()` and `dist_info_name()`. Both validate with `parse_wheel_filename` first, so bad names and non-`.whl` files raise `InvalidWheelFilename`. Name and version come straight from the filename, so `MarkupSafe` stays `MarkupSafe`. Both are exported from `fromager.pkgmetadata`.\n- **`src/fromager/candidate.py`**: `_wheel_metadata_path(url)` takes the last path segment, ignores the query and fragment, and unquotes it. `get_metadata_for_wheel()` reads exactly that member and raises `ValueError` if it's missing.\n- **`src/fromager/wheels.py`**: `extract_info_from_wheel_file` uses `verbatim_dist_name` instead of splitting on `-`.\n- **`src/fromager/dependencies.py`**: `_get_metadata_from_wheel` builds its path with `dist_info_name`, which uses `verbatim_dist_name` internally. I removed the now-unused `parse_wheel_filename` import.\n\n**Tests**\n\n- `tests/test_pkgmetadata.py`: helper tests, including build tags, verbatim casing and version, and rejected filenames.\n- `tests/test_candidate.py` (new): URL path handling, and the fallback path with a vendored `.dist-info` listed first, plus the missing-member error.\n- `tests/test_dependencies.py`: regression test for the vendored `.dist-info` case in `_get_metadata_from_wheel`.\n\n**Choices I made**\n\n- `_wheel_metadata_path` unquotes the filename, so `%2B` in a URL matches the literal `+` in the zip.\n- The helpers let `InvalidWheelFilename` propagate rather than wrapping it.\n\n**Not verified**\n\n- mypy is not usable here: `~/.local/bin/mypy` fails with `No module named 'mypy'`, and `.venv` has neither ruff nor mypy. I ran ruff from PATH for lint and format.\n- I did not run the full test suite, since CLAUDE.md asks for file-scoped runs on small changes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9863,"cache_read_input_tokens":84356,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9863},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9a33c095-6487-48de-97f4-675d9d42443e","uuid":"19dfe031-7243-4834-80bc-af364d172e64","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:34:42.626Z","request_id":"req_011CfrudDGKFAGor11A3ozaJ"}
